\caption(The theoretical truncation bound falls by 14.18 decimal orders per additional mathematical term; it does not bound the floating evaluator's total error.)
\alttext(An orange straight line shows log base ten of a geometric exact-arithmetic truncation bound, from about minus thirteen with one term to about minus 169 with twelve terms.)

> Actual term underflow and very large requests

The scalar evaluator retains constant numeric state; the traced evaluator owns
one record per actual term. Stagnation does not end either computation. They
continue through the first term that underflows to signed zero, include its
addition, and then skip the requested suffix. Multiplying zero by subsequent
finite recurrence factors would keep producing zero. A huge requested count
therefore creates no huge trace reservation on the ordinary binary64 platform.
This stopping reason is a floating range observation, not a real-error test.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::print("| current k | next/current signed ratio | -log10 ratio magnitude |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto k:{0,1,2,10,100,10000,std::numeric_limits<int>::max()}) {
    const auto r=dm::algorithms::chudnovsky_term_ratio(k);
    std::print("| {} | {:.12e} | {:.9f} |\n",k,r,-std::log10(std::fabs(r)));
  }
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::chudnovsky_pi_trace(std::numeric_limits<int>::max());
  if(t.stop!=dm::algorithms::ChudnovskyStop::TermUnderflow || t.steps.back().term!=0)return 1;
  std::print("\nRequested {}, actually evaluated {}, ratio evaluations {}, additions {}, first unchanged index {}.\n",
      t.terms_requested,t.terms_evaluated,t.ratio_evaluations,t.sum_additions,t.first_unchanged_index);
  std::print("\n| last actual k | term | sum changed |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=t.steps.size()-3;i<t.steps.size();++i) {
    const auto& s=t.steps[i];std::print("| {} | {:.12e} | {} |\n",s.index,s.term,s.sum_changed);
  }
  std::print("\nFinal estimate {:.17g}; scalar and trace agree exactly: {}.\n",t.value,t.value==dm::algorithms::chudnovsky_pi(std::numeric_limits<int>::max()));
}
```
